 "response": {
  "text": "If you want **good formal shirts for men in India**, I’d shortlist these brands:\n\n### [Van Heusen Solid Slim Fit Formal Shirt]()\n*₹1,029*\n\n### [Louis Philippe Solid Full Sleeves Formal Shirt]()\n*₹1,724*\n\n### [Raymond Slim Fit Solid Formal Shirt]()\n*₹986*\n\n### [Blackberrys Solid Slim Fit Formal Shirt]()\n*₹2,619*\n\n### [Park Avenue Stripe Cotton Shirt]()\n*₹1,055*\n\n| Brand | Best for | Typical budget |\n|---|---|---:|\n| **Van Heusen** | Best overall/value | ₹1,000–2,500 |\n| **Louis Philippe** | Premium, senior/professional look | ₹1,500–3,500+ |\n| **Raymond** | Classic, conservative formal wear | ₹1,000–3,000 |\n| **Arrow** | Crisp, traditional corporate look | ₹1,500–3,500 |\n| **Blackberrys** | Sharper/slimmer modern fit | ₹1,500–3,500 |\n| **Park Avenue** | Good everyday office wear | ₹800–2,500 |\n| **Peter England** | Budget-friendly wardrobe | ₹700–2,000 |\n\n\nCurrent 2026 comparisons consistently put **Van Heusen, Louis Philippe, Raymond, Arrow, Blackberrys and Park Avenue** among the stronger Indian formalwear choices. [midvey.com](https://midvey.com/blogs/news/top-10-best-formal-shirt-brands-in-india-for-2026?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n### My recommendation\n\n- **₹1,000–1,500:** **Van Heusen or Park Avenue**\n- **₹1,500–2,500:** **Van Heusen or Raymond** — probably the sweet spot\n- **₹2,500–4,000:** **Louis Philippe or Arrow**\n- **Sharper/slimmer styling:** **Blackberrys**\n- **Building a work wardrobe on a budget:** **Peter England**\n\nFor your first few shirts, I'd buy **2 white, 2 light blue, and 1 very subtle blue/grey stripe**. Prioritize **fit and cotton fabric** over the logo—a well-fitting ₹1,500 shirt will generally look better than an expensive shirt in the wrong cut. [www.flickonclick.com](https://www.flickonclick.com/best-formal-shirt-brands/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)\n\n**If you tell me your budget per shirt (e.g. ₹1,000, ₹1,500, ₹2,500) and whether you prefer slim or regular fit, I can pick 5 specific shirts worth buying right now.**",
